Since they started making WFTO in 2010/11 game is finally done. It has 13 campaign missions + 4 in HoG DLC. I think I could reccomend this game, it seems finished, but there are many areas in WFTO that could be extended much futher and still you can encounter bugs & strange performance drops on powerfull computers.
Pros:
- There are many different dungeon (tiles, walls, some rooms for Empire) and worker themes;
- Except rooms, spells and traps you can also place constructions, do rituals and drop potions which makes game more diverse, there are also some new kinds of walls;
- DK 2 mentor has moved to WFTO;
- Customer service, after not very good first releases Devs are now much more into players feedback.
Cons:
- Timed achievments - Do NOT make any timed events if there is no reason to make them, the frustration of repeating levels because few seconds were needed to win the game in time destroys overall joy of playing the game;
- Strange AI - it rushes your dungeon spamming rally flags with poor units which makes it really easy to destroy their dungeon core;
- There's a map editor, however it's limited to making terrains and creatures, no scripting, no campaign editor, so no surprise of something like sudden Empire units dropping out of the ceiling;
- Creature's seems to be hardly distinguished from each other and all Empire units has the same amount of HP, some however like Vampires are way more stronger than others;
- Ambient music makes me want to sleep instead of playing more;
- Game has still some performance problems, i.e. creatures sometimes instead of fighting escape it to fulfill their needs (especially Cultists or Jaggernaut), you can encounter fps drops for no reason.
Pozdrawiam wszystkich, a zwłaszcza ekipę z byłego forum dk.boo.pl. :)

