Lovely soundtrack and superbly simple graphics, though the glitches and small bugs can be annoying at times, it's still a very enjoyable game. I'd definitely ask anyone who has posted a negative review to give the game another go, it's progressing quite quickly. The game does not yet have many features but the developers have assured us there will be more! I can promise you it will be a good game when it's finished but I suppose we'll just have to wait until then! Right now, the game's not OVERLY enjoyable for long lengths of time so I would recommend maybe plopping it on your wishlist for now and maybe purchasing it when the next Steam Summer Sale comes along. That leaves plenty of time for new features to flood in. Anyway I'd certainly recommend this game and for the price - not bad!
I give it a 7.5/10

Game created by Sonic Team for SEGA Saturn. You can really feel the matter of speedrunning and going for perfect scores, espacialy when you have limited time. It has both remastered and oldschool version of the game. I prefer remastered one. I might some day try to master it though it's not easy.
Pros:
- Good game for both casuals (just to pass levels) and hardcores (fully complete);
- Sonic fans might like it;
- Mechanic at first confusing but later on easy to understand;
- Great music.
Cons:
- Honestly I don't know what's bad in this game... IMO I don't like kids in this game but without them the plot would be in chaos.

